  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 817 PM CDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nBy Saturday, upper level ridging from the central CONUS will have \nstretched and amplified up into the Great Lakes region but also \nprogressed east into the Southeast as well. This will largely persist\ninto next week; however, synoptic guidance suggests that this ridge \nwill weaken as a shortwave, moving along the flow of a parent trough \nspanning much of the western CONUS, makes its way over the \nMississippi River Valley on Tuesday. Surface high pressure also looks\nto maintain its hold over the region through most of the long term \nperiod. Although, there is the potential for a trailing front from a \nlow pressure system slated to swing over Canada to slowly push \nsouthward towards the TN Valley on Tuesday. Ultimately, dry weather \nwill comprise much of the forecast through at least Monday, with \ncontinued high temperatures in the 70s and lows in the 40s. Questions\nstill remain regarding any rain chances for Tuesday and into \nmidweek, but we will monitor model trends over the coming days. Make \nsure to check back for updates!",
